The input is a sequence of numbers from 79 to 171 inclusive. The condition is that each of these numbers should have a number evenly divisible by 7 added to the number, ensuring that the final number is the result of this operation having a 6 remainder. So, for each number 'n', calculate (n + 7k) mod 7 where k is an integer such that (n + 7k) % 7 == 6. Then, negate each number from the original list, negating each (n) becomes (-n % 10 == 6). Double this number, so (-n % 10 == 6) becomes (( - ( - n) ) * 2 % 10). So, it's (( ( - n) * 2 % 10) ). After that, the result is simply ( (( - n) * 2 % 10) % 10 = 4 ).

